# Line endings. Added 2026-08-07.
#
# This repo accumulated roughly 300 files whose only difference from HEAD was
# carriage returns, because it is edited from both Windows and Linux tooling.
# Two concrete costs, both hit during the 2026-08-07 session: a 71 line
# addition showed up as a 130 line whole-file rewrite, and `git add -A` is
# unsafe here because it sweeps up hundreds of files nobody meant to touch.
#
# text=auto tells git to normalize to LF in the repository for anything it
# detects as text. eol=lf checks it back out as LF everywhere. Existing drifted
# files are NOT rewritten by this on its own: they normalize the next time each
# one is staged, so the cleanup arrives gradually instead of as one enormous
# commit.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
